// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
// The remount re-grab fact (the clip-focus law's remount half, #1490;
// #1419 option A): the adapter's zero-duration timer — a later
// event-loop turn than the deferred change-handler pass, so the
// rebuild's release and visibility drop have both landed — bumps this
// nonce. The mounted create field consumes it edge-triggered (the
// FocusFacts / FocusScrollHint discipline: a derived property plus a
// `changed`, exactly one consumption per write because the adapter's
// consumed-once arm takes the arm before the write). "When to
// re-grab" is adapter-owned; the nonce carries no decision. A global
// callback cannot route into a model-row instance (slint: callback
// connections parse a single identifier, callback aliases only parse
// at declaration sites — the three bisected compile failures in the
// 2026-11-27 experiments report), so the fact write is the seam.
export global TryRefocus {
    in property <int> create-nonce: 0;
}
